<title>JAPAN: Toyota March domestic output up 18.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Toyota March domestic output up 18.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp said on Monday that its domestic vehicle production rose 18.8 percent in March from a year earlier to 371,903 vehicles.</p>
<p>Toyota's exports fell by 1.1 percent in March from a year earlier to 103,117 vehicles.</p>
<p>Toyota's domestic production rebounded in March after falling in the previous month on a year-on-year basis.</p>
<p>Toyota's domestic sales rose for the seventh month in a row, reflecting persistent strong demand for new recreational vehicles such as its Ipsum, Spacio, Estima series, Prado and Camry Gracia Wagon, he said.  </p>
<p>Toyota's domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in March were as follows:</p>
<p> Production	   371,903  up   18.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		307,604  up   21.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   64,299  up    6.4 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     325,169  up   15.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		227,365  up   17.0 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   97,804  up   13.0 percent</p>
<p> Exports		103,117  down  1.1 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		 74,789  down  0.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses   28,328  down  2.5 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output    126,461  up   14.2 percent</p>
<p>Toyota's domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales and overseas output in the year to March were as follows:</p>
<p> Production	   3,500,782  up   10.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		2,889,573  up   12.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses    611,209  up    0.6 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales     2,214,103  up    7.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		1,490,885  up    7.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses    723,218  up    8.4 percent</p>
<p> Exports		1,311,581  up   12.4 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		  994,522  up   15.8 percent</p>
<p>  - Trucks &amp; buses    317,059  up    3.0 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output    1,378,086  up    7.4 percent</p>
</text>
